#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum optimization {#quantum-optimization}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum optimization explores how quantum computing can be used to solve optimization problems, where the goal is to find the best, or a good, solution among many possible alternatives (often under a set of constraints). Applications of this field include logistics and scheduling, portfolio optimization, and protein folding.\n"
"Quantum optimization approaches include quantum approximate optimization algorithms (QAOA) and other hybrid quantum-classical methods that combine quantum processors with classical optimization techniques. Although quantum computing has the potential to augment our ability to solve optimization problems, identifying practical performance benefits over classical methods remains an active area of research.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Solving an optimization problem on a quantum computer generally involves two"
" stages. First, formulate the problem, (for example, as a quadratic "
"unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problem, a higher-order binary "
"optimization (HUBO) problem, or a problem with explicit constraints), and "
"map that formulation into quantum operators and circuits. Second, run the "
"resulting circuit on quantum hardware and interpret the measurement results "
"as a candidate solution. The tools on this page support these two stages: "
"the mapping tool helps you move from a problem definition to a quantum-ready"
" representation, and the application functions combine mapping, hardware "
"execution, and classical post-processing into a single managed workflow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mapping tools {#mapping-tools}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This capability specializes in mapping domain problems into quantum "
"operators and circuits for execution on a quantum computer. Use it to "
"formulate an optimization problem as a binary model, convert that model "
"between representations, and validate it against classical solvers before "
"running on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""

